{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's prop names."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-inputs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text inputs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many Svelte text-input components accept DOM-like props:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.Field name=\"name\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    <TextInput\n      name={field.name}\n      label=\"Name\"\n      value={field.value}\n      onblur={field.handleBlur}\n      oninput={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.value)}\n      error={field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of using a component's one-time default-value prop so the\ncomponent reflects form state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checkboxes and switches"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DOM-style checkbox components expose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.currentTarget.checked"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.Field name=\"acceptedTerms\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    <Checkbox\n      checked={field.value}\n      onblur={field.handleBlur}\n      onchange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.checked)}\n      aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some libraries call back with a boolean, a details object, or a union such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean | 'indeterminate'"},{"type":"text","value":". Normalize that value at the boundary:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Checkbox\n  checked={field.value}\n  onCheckedChange={(checked) => field.handleChange(checked === true)}\n/>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The integration does not require a native event. Pass the value produced by the\ncomponent to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleChange"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<DatePicker\n  value={field.value}\n  onValueChange={(nextDate) => field.handleChange(nextDate)}\n  onblur={field.handleBlur}\n/>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reuse-the-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reuse the adapter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a Svelte\ncomponent that accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldWithValue<T>"},{"type":"text","value":" or register it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFormHook"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../splitting-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splitting forms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The repository's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/svelte/large-form"},{"type":"text","value":" example demonstrates reusable\nfield and form components with the v2 Svelte adapter."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"text-inputs","text":"Text inputs","level":2},{"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","text":"Checkboxes and switches","level":2},{"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","text":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls","level":2},{"id":"reuse-the-adapter","text":"Reuse the adapter","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's prop names.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nMany Svelte text-input components accept DOM-like props:\n\n```svelte\n<form.Field name=\"name\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    <TextInput\n      name={field.name}\n      label=\"Name\"\n      value={field.value}\n      onblur={field.handleBlur}\n      oninput={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.value)}\n      error={field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nPass `value` instead of using a component's one-time default-value prop so the\ncomponent reflects form state.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nDOM-style checkbox components expose `event.currentTarget.checked`:\n\n```svelte\n<form.Field name=\"acceptedTerms\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    <Checkbox\n      checked={field.value}\n      onblur={field.handleBlur}\n      onchange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.checked)}\n      aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nSome libraries call back with a boolean, a details object, or a union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize that value at the boundary:\n\n```svelte\n<Checkbox\n  checked={field.value}\n  onCheckedChange={(checked) => field.handleChange(checked === true)}\n/>\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value produced by the\ncomponent to `field.handleChange`:\n\n```svelte\n<DatePicker\n  value={field.value}\n  onValueChange={(nextDate) => field.handleChange(nextDate)}\n  onblur={field.handleBlur}\n/>\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nIf the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a Svelte\ncomponent that accepts `FieldWithValue<T>` or register it with\n`createFormHook`.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nThe repository's `examples/svelte/large-form` example demonstrates reusable\nfield and form components with the v2 Svelte adapter.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ui-libraries\ntitle: UI Libraries\n---\n\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's prop names.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nMany Svelte text-input components accept DOM-like props:\n\n```svelte\n<form.Field name=\"name\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    <TextInput\n      name={field.name}\n      label=\"Name\"\n      value={field.value}\n      onblur={field.handleBlur}\n      oninput={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.value)}\n      error={field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nPass `value` instead of using a component's one-time default-value prop so the\ncomponent reflects form state.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nDOM-style checkbox components expose `event.currentTarget.checked`:\n\n```svelte\n<form.Field name=\"acceptedTerms\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    <Checkbox\n      checked={field.value}\n      onblur={field.handleBlur}\n      onchange={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.checked)}\n      aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nSome libraries call back with a boolean, a details object, or a union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize that value at the boundary:\n\n```svelte\n<Checkbox\n  checked={field.value}\n  onCheckedChange={(checked) => field.handleChange(checked === true)}\n/>\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value produced by the\ncomponent to `field.handleChange`:\n\n```svelte\n<DatePicker\n  value={field.value}\n  onValueChange={(nextDate) => field.handleChange(nextDate)}\n  onblur={field.handleBlur}\n/>\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nIf the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a Svelte\ncomponent that accepts `FieldWithValue<T>` or register it with\n`createFormHook`.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nThe repository's `examples/svelte/large-form` example demonstrates reusable\nfield and form components with the v2 Svelte adapter.\n"}
